	"title"		"Viewpoint Extended Support"
	"description"		"[h1]Viewpoint Extended Support[/h1] Quality-of-life and compatibility features for Project Viewpoint in Project Zomboid Build 42.20+. [h2]Camera and mouse[/h2] [list][*]Choose a vehicle camera mode: force third person in the vehicle and return to first person on exit, preserve the previous perspective while driving and restore it afterward, or disable camera switching.[*]Hold Mouse Button 4 for free mouse control; customize the bind and its Shift, Ctrl, or Alt modifiers.[*]Automatically release and center the mouse when opening an inventory or supported menu; it stays free while the interface is open and centers again when reopened.[*]Preserves Viewpoint's native middle-mouse cursor toggle.[*]Supports vanilla and Ergonomic UI inventories, prioritizes inventory scrolling, and can hide the Viewpoint interaction menu while an inventory is open.[*]Keeps mouse look and interaction available for collapsed inventory panels.[/list] [h2]Interaction improvements[/h2] [list][*]Shows what you are interacting with in the heading, such as [i]Interact with Ground[/i].[*]Cycle nearby interaction targets with Left/Right arrows or Alt+Scroll; binds and modifiers are configurable.[*]Optional cascading interaction menus, including container contents, with deferred [i]View options[/i] loading.[*]Preserves vanilla interaction icons and optionally integrates with Simple Context Menu Icons.[/list] [h2]Project A-Life support[/h2] [list][*]NPC speech bubbles and the Answer prompt follow the NPC in Viewpoint's camera view.[*]Talk and trade actions target the NPC you are aiming at, avoiding options from other nearby NPCs.[*]Hides Viewpoint's interaction panel during conversations and releases the mouse for dialogue; restores mouse control when the conversation closes.[*]These features are optional and require Project A-Life; Project Viewpoint QOL can also restore camera control after conversations.[/list] [h2]Other integrations[/h2] [list][*]Companion Dogs: camera-aware name tags and exclusion of Friendly and Allied A-Life NPCs from threat detection.[*]Wolf Extraction Quest: optionally start the Extraction Tracker closed when loading a save.[/list] [h2]Configuration and requirements[/h2] Configure features and key binds in the categorized in-game Mod Options. Automatic Viewpoint startup, skipping the setup screen, and diagnostic logging are disabled by default. Requires Project Viewpoint, ZombieBuddy 2.3.0 or newer, and Project Zomboid Build 42.20+. Other supported mods are optional and needed only for their respective integrations. [h2]Latest update[/h2] [list][*]Choose whether to hide Viewpoint's interaction menu while an inventory is open and reserve mouse-wheel scrolling for the inventory; enabled by default.[*]Optionally disable Viewpoint's yellow target outline in Mod Options; the outline remains enabled by default.[/list]\n\nWorkshop ID: 3812978679\nMod ID: ViewpointExtendedSupport"
	"changenote"		"0.4.46: Make inventory scroll priority configurable and add an optional target-outline toggle."
}
